    "number": "Theorem 1",
    "quote": "Let the assumptions of Proposition \\ref{prop:prop_upper_bound_lpe} hold. For $i=1,\\dots,T$, let $\\hat{x}_i$ be a minimizer over $[0,1]^d$ of the local polynomial estimator $\\hat{f}\\exponentalpha_i$. Then there exists a constant $C>0$ such that \n\\begin{equation*}\n    \\sup_{f\\in\\betahold}\\Exp_f\\goodbrak{f\\exponentalpha(\\hat{x}_T) - \\min_{x\\in[0,1]^d}f\\exponentalpha(x)} \\leq C \\goodpar{\\frac{\\log(T)}{T}}^{\\fracbeta{\\beta-k}},\n\\end{equation*}"
   },
   "confidence": "high",
   "notes": "Simple regret of output point; constant C unspecified. Paper says the exact minimizer is in general not computable in polynomial time."
  },
